{
    "background_story": "Esther was a gentle giant, a brown bear who roamed the forests of the Pacific Northwest. As winter approached, she began to prepare for her long slumber, a state of torpor that would see her through the harsh months ahead. Esther's body slowed, her heart rate dropping dramatically as she settled into her cozy den. She spent the winter in a state of reduced activity, her body conserving energy as the snow piled up outside. During this time, Esther's dreams were filled with visions of the spring to come, when she would emerge from her den and start anew. As the days lengthened and the weather warmed, Esther slowly stirred, stretching her limbs and shaking off the torpor. She emerged from her den, blinking in the bright sunlight, ready to start another year of exploration and discovery in the forest she called home.",
